IMPORT prelude

-- Little Sisters of the Poor Ordinance 1957 (Singapore) -- who the Corporation "Reverend Mother Superior of the Little Sisters of
-- the Poor in Malaya" is (s 2(1)), what the Ordinance empowers it to do (s 2(2), (3)), how its deeds are validly sealed and signed
-- (s 3), what a Gazette notification proves (s 4), and whose rights the Ordinance leaves alone (s 5).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/LSPO1957.txt. The deposit says the edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". The only amendment
-- annotation in the body is "[7/97]" under s 5. The Ordinance is dated 1 November 1957. Section numbers follow the body (s 1 short
-- title to s 5 saving); the arrangement at the top of the deposit is shifted by the PDF extraction (it prints "1." with no heading and
-- puts each heading against the following number) but carries the same five headings.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0237 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 4 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance. It asks what the Ordinance decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper question yet.
-- The Ordinance is five sections long, so the whole of it is in scope. For a person outside the Congregation it matters mainly when
-- buying, leasing or lending on the security of the Corporation's property (s 2(3)), and in checking that the Corporation's deed was
-- executed by the right person (ss 3, 4).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 1 (short title); the recitals (Rennes 1839, the Home at 999 Thomson Road, Penang), which are quoted in NOTES.md but
-- decide nothing; the content of s 48 of the Conveyancing and Law of Property Act 1886, to which s 3(1) refers (whether a power of
-- attorney has been "deposited" under it is taken as a stated fact); how a Reverend Mother Superior is appointed, which s 2(1) says is
-- "hereinafter provided" but which the Ordinance never provides; the Corporation's internal governance.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Little Sisters of the Poor Ordinance 1957 -- the Corporation`

§§ `2(1) and 4 -- who is the Corporation, and what a notice in the Gazette proves`

-- s 2(1): "The said Reverend Mother Hedwige and her successors for the time being in office of the Reverend Mother Superior of the
-- Little Sisters of the Poor in Malaya, duly authorised and appointed as hereinafter provided, shall be a body corporate", called the
-- "Corporation", with the name "Reverend Mother Superior of the Little Sisters of the Poor in Malaya", perpetual succession and a
-- corporate seal.
-- s 4: "A notification in the Gazette of the appointment of any person to exercise the office of Reverend Mother Superior of the
-- Little Sisters of the Poor in Malaya shall be conclusive evidence that such person was duly authorised to exercise the said office."
--
-- Nothing after s 2(1) says how a successor is "authorised and appointed". The only later provision about appointment is s 4, which is
-- about proof, not about the appointing. So the encoding treats the Corporation's holder as whoever is "for the time being in office"
-- and "duly authorised"; the Gazette proves authorisation conclusively. Without a notice, authorisation is a matter of other evidence,
-- which the Ordinance does not regulate (so the encoding returns FALSE for "conclusively proved", not "not authorised").
DECLARE Office IS ONE OF
    `Reverend Mother Superior`
    `some other office in the Congregation`

GIVEN `the office` IS AN Office, `the appointment is notified in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `authorisation is conclusively proved` IF
        `the appointment is notified in the Gazette`
    AND CONSIDER `the office`
        WHEN `Reverend Mother Superior` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `is for the time being in office` IS A BOOLEAN, `is duly authorised and appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `holds the corporate office` IF
    `is for the time being in office` AND `is duly authorised and appointed`

§§ `2(2) and 2(3) -- what the Ordinance empowers the Corporation to do`

-- s 2(2): "The said seal may from time to time be broken, changed, altered and made anew as the Corporation thinks fit."
-- s 2(3): the Corporation "may acquire, purchase, take, hold and enjoy movable and immovable property of every description, and may
-- sell, convey, assign, surrender and yield up, mortgage, demise, re-assign, transfer or otherwise dispose of any movable and immovable
-- property vested in the Corporation upon such terms as the Corporation shall think fit."
--
-- The powers of disposal reach only property "vested in the Corporation". Unlike some sibling incorporation ordinances, this one gives
-- no express capacity to sue or be sued; the Ordinance grants no power beyond s 2 (whether the general law of corporations supplies one
-- is outside the text and not encoded, so those powers return FALSE as "not granted by the Ordinance"). "Exchange" is not in the list;
-- it is treated here as covered by "otherwise dispose of" (an inference).
DECLARE Power IS ONE OF
    `use and change its corporate seal`
    `acquire or purchase property`
    `hold and enjoy property`
    `sell property`
    `mortgage property`
    `lease property`
    `surrender property`
    `exchange or otherwise dispose of property`
    `sue in respect of its property`
    `be sued in respect of its property`
    `borrow money without security`

GIVEN `the power` IS A Power, `the property is vested in the Corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Ordinance empowers the Corporation to` IF
    CONSIDER `the power`
    WHEN `use and change its corporate seal` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `acquire or purchase property` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `hold and enjoy property` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sell property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `mortgage property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `lease property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `surrender property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `exchange or otherwise dispose of property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `3 -- sealing and signing the Corporation's instruments`

-- s 3(1): "All deeds, documents and other instruments requiring the seal of the Corporation shall be sealed with the seal of the
-- Corporation in the presence of the Reverend Mother Superior for the time being or her attorney, duly authorised by power of attorney
-- deposited under section 48 of the Conveyancing and Law of Property Act 1886, and shall also be signed by the said Reverend Mother
-- Superior for the time being, or her attorney so authorised as aforesaid."
-- s 3(2): "Such signing shall be and be taken as sufficient evidence that the said seal was duly and properly affixed and that the
-- same is the lawful seal of the Corporation."
--
-- Readings encoded (inferences from the wording, not stated):
--   * Only the Reverend Mother Superior "for the time being" qualifies; a former holder does not.
--   * "her attorney" is read as the attorney of the Reverend Mother Superior for the time being, so it presupposes a holder in office.
--     The Ordinance makes no provision for a vacancy (no deputy or stand-in is named), so while the office is vacant nobody qualifies
--     under s 3(1). Whether a power granted by the previous holder survives her leaving office is not addressed by the text.
--   * An attorney whose power was not deposited never qualifies.
--   * The witness and the signer need not be the same person: the text allows "the Reverend Mother Superior ... or her attorney" for
--     each, separately.
DECLARE Officer IS ONE OF
    `the Reverend Mother Superior for the time being`
    `an attorney under a deposited power of attorney`
    `an attorney whose power of attorney is not deposited`
    `a former Reverend Mother Superior`
    `another Sister`
    `nobody`

DECLARE Instrument HAS
    `is sealed with the Corporation seal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sealed in the presence of` IS AN Officer
    `signed by` IS AN Officer

GIVEN `the officer` IS AN Officer, `the office is filled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may act for the Corporation under section 3` IF
        `the office is filled`
    AND CONSIDER `the officer`
        WHEN `the Reverend Mother Superior for the time being` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `an attorney under a deposited power of attorney` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument, `the office is filled now` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is executed as section 3 requires` IF
        `the instrument`'s `is sealed with the Corporation seal`
    AND `may act for the Corporation under section 3` (`the instrument`'s `sealed in the presence of`) `the office is filled now`
    AND `may act for the Corporation under section 3` (`the instrument`'s `signed by`) `the office is filled now`

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument, `the office is filled now` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the signature is sufficient evidence the seal was duly affixed` IF
        `the instrument`'s `is sealed with the Corporation seal`
    AND `may act for the Corporation under section 3` (`the instrument`'s `signed by`) `the office is filled now`

§§ `5 -- whose rights are saved`

-- s 5: "Nothing in this Ordinance shall affect the rights of the Government, all bodies politic and corporate, and all others except
-- such as are expressly mentioned in this Ordinance, and those claiming by, from or under them."
GIVEN `is expressly mentioned in the Ordinance` IS A BOOLEAN, `claims by, from or under a person mentioned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Ordinance may affect their rights` IF
    `is expressly mentioned in the Ordinance` OR `claims by, from or under a person mentioned`
